1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,144
My landlord doesn't want my money. He wants my very first birthday party, paid in full today.

2
00:00:06,444 --> 00:00:16,164
Maya, a 25-year-old woman with messy dark hair and a faded yellow sweater, hands over the glowing orb of cake and laughter.

3
00:00:16,464 --> 00:00:23,928
The old man swallows the light. Instantly, my mind goes blank. The chocolate cake? Never existed.

4
00:00:24,228 --> 00:00:33,036
Rent is due every week. If the account is empty, you vanish from this world completely. No exceptions.

5
00:00:33,336 --> 00:00:42,048
I search my brain for anything left. Summer rain, first kisses, my mother's warm embrace on cold nights.

6
00:00:42,348 --> 00:00:48,516
He knocks again. Next month's price is steep. He demands the day I learned how to ride a bike.

7
00:00:48,816 --> 00:00:55,176
I refuse to give it up. I pull back his sleeve to see why he needs my joy so badly.

8
00:00:55,476 --> 00:01:01,548
There is a scar on his arm. The exact same jagged scar I received when I fell at age ten.

9
00:01:01,848 --> 00:01:08,640
He looks at me with hollow, weeping eyes. He whispers that this is the only way we survive.

10
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:13,236
If I pay this month's rent with my past, who will I be tomorrow?
